  "fresh_tests_excluding_overlapping_selected_run": 683,
  "ignored_tests": "Three standalone Store crash helpers are ignored as individual cases and invoked by their passing parent tests.",
  "implemented": [
    "Exact current independent operator, original native source and retained authority feed Prepare-only ParticipantReplacementControl.",
    "One durable begin invokes one real Core owned DeviceReplacementPreparation. Actual binding/appearance/role are captured; recording retries never invoke Core again.",
    "No authority reader survives in the ticket or worker between bounded actions; nonblocking current polling tolerates transient writer contention.",
    "Public cancel, current controller revocation and provisioned target revocation cancel only the actual uncommitted preparation; original native media and roles remain intact.",
    "Idempotent protected local-stop capture is allowed after controller revocation and refuses if any non-prepare step began.",
    "Definitive exact-command refusal before reservation cannot close reserved or possibly invoked work.",
    "Ordinary native preparation cannot take a replacement-reserved logical candidate ID before or after cancellation.",
    "Released Core preparation capacity is reused by a distinct later root in both speaking and observer scenarios. Reserved candidate IDs remain tombstoned."
  ],
  "unqualified": [
    "Target signed allocation and replacement binding lineage/generation adoption",
    "Independent allocate/start/commit attempt APIs",
    "Actual isolated target duplex and trusted configured answer/DTMF",
    "Managed movement commit, native confirmation, durable projection and intended old-source retirement",
    "No-answer, voicemail, rejected confirmation, callback timeout, unknown submission/no redial and complete late-event/restart matrix",
    "Gate6 acceptance, remote/provider/performance scopes and publication"
